        "These are historical amounts from one person's experience and one local labour market. They are not current wage guidance.\nWhy a job can support entrepreneurship\nA job can provide three things that an uncertain side hustle may not:\n1. Reliable cash flow: money to cover expenses and build a small reserve.\n2. A learning environment: exposure to customers, operations, sales, and service delivery.\n3. A lower-pressure testing ground: the ability to test a business without depending on it immediately for every living expense.\nEmployment is not the opposite of entrepreneurship. It can finance the early experiments that make entrepreneurship possible.\nMove toward higher-value work when you can\nThe transition from hourly work to auto-glass sales is particularly instructive. Instead of only performing the physical service of cleaning cars, the operator moved into selling windshield repair or replacement services and earning commissions.",
