        "Commission-based roles can teach:\n- Prospecting.\n- Starting conversations.\n- Explaining value.\n- Handling objections.\n- Following up.\n- Asking for a decision.\n- Understanding conversion rates.\nThese skills transfer directly to running a business.\nDo not confuse commission potential with guaranteed income\nBefore accepting a commission-based role, understand:\n- Whether there is a base wage.\n- How commissions are calculated.\n- When commissions are paid.\n- Whether refunds or cancellations affect them.\n- Whether leads are supplied.\n- What expenses you must cover.\n- Whether the product and sales claims are legitimate.\nA high advertised commission is not useful if sales are rare, payment is delayed, or the product is poor.\nA simple capital-building system\nWhen income arrives, divide it deliberately:\n- Essential expenses.\n- Emergency reserve.\n- Business testing budget.\n- Long-term savings.\nDo not put every dollar into a new idea. Keep enough cash to handle ordinary expenses and unexpected problems.",
