        "The lesson is not that education or real estate is a bad choice. It is that a business model must fit your current resources, skills, credibility, and time horizon.\nEvaluate a new path before committing\nAsk:\n- How long before the first realistic payment?\n- What qualifications or licences are required?\n- What does training cost?\n- How will I find customers?\n- What proof of competence will customers expect?\n- Can I keep earning while I learn?\n- What happens if the first few months produce no income?\nUse a bridge strategy\nWhen exploring a new career or business, consider maintaining a source of income while testing the new direction.",
