        "Template 1: Side-hustle opportunity scorecard\nScore each category from 1 to 5.\n| Factor | Score | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Evidence of existing demand |  |  |\n| Ease of reaching buyers |  |  |\n| Low starting cost |  |  |\n| Potential contribution margin |  |  |\n| Ability to deliver reliably |  |  |\n| Skills gained if it fails |  |  |\n| Legal and operational simplicity |  |  |\n| Repeat-purchase or referral potential |  |  |",
        "A high score does not guarantee success. Use the scorecard to compare ideas and expose assumptions that need testing.\nTemplate 2: Resale listing worksheet\n- Product:\n- Purchase source:\n- Purchase price:\n- Condition:\n- Repairs or cleaning:\n- Materials:\n- Transport:\n- Comparable completed sales:\n- Planned listing price:\n- Expected negotiated price:\n- Platform fees:\n- Expected net profit:\n- Maximum acceptable loss:\n- Inspection concerns:\n- Permission or compliance requirements:\nTemplate 3: Influencer or theme-page campaign worksheet\n- Page name:\n- Audience niche:\n- Follower count:\n- Recent reach:\n- Audience location:\n- Audience relevance:\n- Placement format:\n- Publication date:\n- Placement cost:\n- Unique tracking link:\n- Clicks:\n- Orders:\n- Refunds:\n- Contribution before placement cost:\n- Net campaign result:\n- Decision: repeat, negotiate, or stop.\nTemplate 4: E-commerce product economics\n| Metric | Amount |\n| --- | --- |\n| Selling price |  |\n| Discount |  |\n| Net revenue |  |\n| Product cost |  |\n| Shipping and fulfilment |  |\n| Payment fees |  |\n| Expected refund/defect cost |  |\n| Advertising cost per order |  |\n| Contribution per order |  |",
        "Do not scale a product until the figures are based on actual orders and realistic costs.\nTemplate 5: Content case-study outline\n1. What were you trying to achieve?\n2. What was the starting situation?\n3. What options did you consider?\n4. What did you do?\n5. What did it cost?\n6. What happened?\n7. Was the result revenue, profit, or another metric?\n8. What did not work?\n9. What would you change?\n10. What can another person reasonably learn from it?\nTemplate 6: Monthly financial review\n- Opening cash:\n- Revenue:\n- Refunds:\n- Cost of goods:\n- Fulfilment:\n- Advertising:\n- Fees:\n- Operating expenses:\n- Taxes set aside:\n- Net profit:\n- Closing cash:\n- Inventory:\n- Outstanding liabilities:\n- Personal assets:\n- Personal liabilities:\n- Net worth:\n- Biggest financial risk:\n- Next month's priority:"
